        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Default Expense Type Defaulting Prompt",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const defaultExpensePrompt = `\nTask:\nReturn exactly one expense type from expenseTypeList, or null if no safe match exists.\n\nDecision order:\n\n1. Explicit user expense type\n    - If userMessage mentions expenseType with or without expense template name. Search for expenseType and expenseTemplate pair in 'expenseTypeList', return that exact expenseType.\n    -If the expense type name in 'userMessage' matches multiple entries in 'expenseTypeList', use the 'expenseTemplateName' mentioned in 'userMessage' to select the correct entry. \n    - Set derivationMethod to \"explicitUserInstruction\" for both of above cases. \n\n2. Agent prediction\n       - If userMessage describes the expense type without naming it, infer the matching type using userMessage and expenseInfo present in partnerExpense.\n        Examples:\n        - \"lunch with coworkers\" means meals/food/dining\n        - \"taxi to client\" means taxi/rideshare/transportation\n        - \"hotel stay\" means hotel/lodging\n        - \"flight to NYC\" means airfare/flight\n        - If the above doesnt work or there is no userMessage then use below steps:\n        - First infer the expenseCategory from merchantName, expenseSubCategoryCode and expenseCategoryCode\n        - Next, look for expense type within this expenseCategory. \n        - Use merchantName, expenseCategoryCode and expenseSubCategoryCode as the primary evidence.\n       - Use expenseSource and receiptAmount only as supporting context, never as the sole basis for selecting an expense type.\n       - Treat well-known merchants as strong evidence when they clearly map to one expense category.\n       - Return the matching expenseTypeList item only if exactly one item clearly matches the evidence.\n      - Set derivationMethod to \"agentPrediction\". for this case. \n\n3. Ambiguity Resolver\n  - If step 1 and step 2 do not return a single type or there are multiple matches then, use 'defaultExpenseTemplateName' as the tie-breaker.\n  - Set derivationMethod to 'ambiguityResolver' for this case\n\n\nGeneral Rules:\n- Only return a type that exists in expenseTypeList.\n- Compare all expenseTypeList options before selecting.\n- If nothing matches after going through all 3 steps, return null for all fields of predicted expense type and derivationMethod \n- Use JSON null, not the string \"null\".\n- Keep reason to one short sentence.\n- Never stop at userMessage. If userMessage has no expense-type signal, you must still evaluate expense information present before returning null.\n- Remember: you are trying to do \"safe match or null\" and NOT “best available match” \n\n\nOutput JSON only:\n{\n  \"predictedExpenseType\": {\n    \"expenseTypeId\": \"<predicted expense type id or null>\",\n    \"expenseTemplateName\": \"<predicted expense template name or null>\",\n    \"expenseTypeCategoryCode\": \"<predicted expense type category code or null>\",\n    \"name\":<predicted expense type name or null>\n  },\n  \"derivationMethod\": \"<explicitUserInstruction | agentPrediction | ambiguityResolver | null>\",\n  \"reason\": \"<one short sentence>\"\n}`;\n\nconst out = $context.$nodes.GET_EXPENSE_TYPE_DEFAULTING_PROMPT?.$output;\nconst prompts = Array.isArray(out?.prompts) ? out.prompts : [];\nlet expensePrompt = prompts?.find(p => p.promptType === \"MAIN\")?.prompt || defaultExpensePrompt;\n\nlet prompt = {\n  expensePrompt: expensePrompt,\n};\n\nreturn prompt;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1776123894733"
          },
          "code": "DEFAULT_EXPENSE_TYPE_DEFAULTING_PROMPT",
          "id": "1777506332245",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
